# CodeLingo Support

CodeLingo is a macOS developer utility for translating English technical text, explaining compiler and runtime errors, and generating code comments.

## Get help

- Report a problem: [Open a support request](https://github.com/hudongsheng-debug/Xcode-Lingo/issues/new)
- View existing reports: [Support requests](https://github.com/hudongsheng-debug/Xcode-Lingo/issues)
- Privacy questions: see the [Privacy Policy](PRIVACY.md)

When requesting support, include the macOS version, CodeLingo version, selected processing mode, expected result, and actual result. Remove API keys, access tokens, private source code, and personal information before posting.

## Common questions

### The Source Editor commands do not appear

Open CodeLingo once. Then open System Settings > General > Login Items & Extensions > Xcode Source Editor, enable CodeLingo Source Editor, and restart Xcode.

### Apple Intelligence is unavailable

Confirm that the Mac and macOS version support Apple Intelligence, that Apple Intelligence is enabled in System Settings, and that its on-device models have finished downloading.

### Cloud processing is unavailable

Cloud processing is optional and disabled by default. Enable it in CodeLingo Settings and provide a compatible endpoint, model name, and API key.

## Response time

Support requests are normally reviewed within five business days.

